Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:43:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] 1.3.95: the patch's Transpose heard, a patch sent whole
 in one command, values past their range held

- TRANSPOSE (the DX7's TRNSP, 24 C3) moves the voice's pitch and its key scaling (fm_note_on, fm_voice): 214 of the
  512 voices of the factory ROMs and the banks sent played an octave or two off; the Transpose knob did nothing
- a patch goes to the engine whole through each voice's mailbox (en_patch_load, a count either side: the engine keeps
  the newest), one command instead of 156: a piece was some 640, so two quick turns of PRESETS could overrun the
  queue of 1024 and drop patch bytes unheard
- a bank's voice, a DX7 single voice and a saved patch: a value past its range held to it, not refused (an old bank's
  stray 127s; one byte no longer drops every piece's patches); erased or empty slots still no voice
- the Patch knob names a bank voice as the piece keeps it, not as the bank holds it since
- an external clock's tempo, measured a beat at a time (en_tempo), drives what hangs on the tempo: the step, the echo,
  SYNC Tempo, the bells' beat and Gate; the clock gone, Tempo's again
- the header names the voice and its page as SELECT turns them, not only on the button
- static checks: the command's 8-bit parameter index and patch offset

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
